>> title: Pomegranate Citrus Salad
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 minutes
>> tags: exotic, watchme, fruit, salad, prep-heavy

-- watch: Pomegranate skin is scored along the pale ridges without cutting into many seeds.
Score @pomegranate{1} from crown to base along the natural ridges with a #paring knife{}.

-- watch: Sections pull apart cleanly and most white pith stays attached to the peel.
Break the pomegranate into sections inside a #bowl{} of water and soak for ~{2%minutes}.

-- watch: Red arils sink while loose white pith floats.
Loosen the arils with your fingers, skim away pith, and drain.

Cut peel and white pith from @oranges{2}, then slice into rounds.

Whisk @olive oil{3%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @honey{1%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} in a #small bowl{}.

Arrange @arugula{4%cups}, orange slices, pomegranate arils, @mint leaves{1/4%cup}, and dressing on a #platter{}.
